# Gitleaks fingerprints that are confirmed non-secrets. One per line, with the
# reason. The fingerprint is commit:file:rule:line, exactly as the gitleaks
# report prints it. The weekly scheduled scan (gitleaks.yml, cron, fetch-depth 0,
# no --log-opts) covers the FULL history, so a historical false positive fails
# that run even after the line itself is gone from HEAD.
#
# README.md at 26a60478 (2026-08-12), curl example in the "Try without a key"
# section: `Authorization: Bearer apier_sandbox_test_<12 random letters>`. That
# is the self-invented sandbox bearer the surrounding prose describes ("any
# suffix after apier_sandbox_test_ works"). It is not a credential: the sandbox
# auth mirror accepts any apier_sandbox_test_ suffix, bypasses the api_keys
# lookup and never calls a government upstream, so there is nothing to rotate.
# The literal appears once in history and nowhere on HEAD. Flagged by the
# default curl-auth-header rule once this repo started extending the default
# ruleset (K14, CS9, PR #57).
